  "minute": "15:00. The minute records the incident as the packets put it: P1 with counsel Day 93 09:10, late against Day 92 10:10; P2 with counsel Day 93 15:20, late against Day 93 14:00, not straight to its recipients; P3 with the chair Day 94 14:30, late against Day 94 11:00. The decisions, each with its decider: the copies paused (Edda, Day 92 07:40); the off-site gap while they are paused (Edda, Day 92 08:05: accepted until the copies resume); the written request to Wellhollow to preserve its logs (Noor, Day 92 11:00); any notice for the town (Noor, her determination Day 93 15:00, N-3 due Day 107 15:00); each member’s notice (its own counsel); any report to law enforcement (Noor for the town and the shared services, each member’s counsel for its own); the statement (the chair, Day 94 12:00, on Noor’s and Ada’s advice). No correction asked. Decided in this minute, this Board the decider of record: the payroll supplier’s transfer account back in service (Marit, Day 74), breaking this Board’s privacy tolerance, which ran on its owner’s acceptance alone from Day 74, past its five-working-day mark (Day 81), before this rule: now this Board’s decision of record, carried to its Day 155 review, its interim measures kept. Reported to this Board, above appetite but within its tolerances, each its owner’s: the airport’s directory trust (Joanna, Day 66). From today, an owner’s acceptance that breaks one of this Board’s tolerances goes to the chair (or, if the chair signed it or is absent, the vice-chair) within five working days of its signing, and into this Board’s next minute; an owner’s acceptance above appetite but within tolerance is reported to this Board at its next meeting. (game)",
  "statement": {
   "by": "Ivor Penhallow",
   "day": 94,
   "at": "12:00",
